From 7379eea71418046f447b818859a96ad3829461b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:46:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] player information: the colour of the film is that of its own
 picture with Dolby Vision converted or native, and profile 5 is IPT-PQ-c2

The line of colour of the film, its matrix and its mastering display
(hades.video.color, hades.video.matrix, hades.src.mastering) say what the
file carries: CWinSystemGbm::SourceColour, which SetHDR() notes from the
picture it is given. For Dolby Vision rebuilt for the output, the
renderer gives it the picture made for the output: the line said BT.2020
PQ, or BT.709 where it is mapped to SDR, whatever the film was; for
native Dolby Vision it is given none, and the line was left out. The
renderer now tells the picture of the video in both cases
(CLinuxRendererGLES::Configure(), NoteSourceColour(), once for each
configuration: no work for each picture), as it does for HDR10 and HLG
mapped to SDR or adapted to the display.

The base layer of profiles 7 and 8 is BT.2020 PQ, and says so. That of
profile 5 (and 10.0) is no picture by itself: it is coded in IPT-PQ-c2,
which the tags of its pictures do not say (they say nothing, and Kodi
takes primaries by the size of the picture). Such a film is named
IPT-PQ-c2, with no matrix, which IPT-PQ-c2 has of its own
(PLAYERINFO::FilmColourOf(), from the configuration record of the stream
and DVBRIDGE::BaseLayerIsNoPicture()). hades.video.colorkind says
"iptpqc2", and Estuary shows its own string, 32754, in English and in
the three Spanish files ($ADDON[skin.estuary 32754]); hades.video.color
has the English name for what reads it without the skin. The pages of
Hades for other skins are made again from Estuary's
(tools/hades-playerinfo).
